From dcdb0868d897ab574b321df3c3627ebfd0443221 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan McIntyre <ewan3568@me.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:51:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Trip builder: pay the rest your way (now, a week before,
 or instalments)

Once the crew approves a trip, the deposit already paid counts and the guest chooses
how to pay the balance, the same way ALL IN bookings work:
  - all now (Stripe Checkout)
  - charged to the card the deposit was paid with, 7 days before they leave
  - instalments when they leave 60+ days out: first now, then every 30 days (up to 6, $20+ each)

- The deposit checkout saves the card (customer_creation + setup_future_usage)
- Approving records the balance and emails "choose how to pay". No Stripe link is made at
  approval any more (those expired in 24h); Checkout is made when the guest chooses
- trip-builder-pay: the guest picks a plan (guest key, one trip, 90 days)
- trip-builder-status: returns the options and schedule for a guest with their key
- charge-trip-builder-payments: daily job (cron, 03:00 UTC): 3-day reminders, off-session charges
  with idempotency keys, retries every 2 days up to 4 times, never after departure
- stripe-webhook / handleTripBuilderPaid: instalment payments, booking on first payment
- New emails: booked, reminder, receipt, payment failed; the ready email lists the choices
- Admin > Trip builder shows each guest's plan and payment progress; a trip that has been paid
  towards can't be declined from the review page
- Migration adds stripe_customer_id, stripe_payment_method_id, pay_plan, pay_schedule, plan_chosen_at
  and schedules the job. Rules live in _shared/trip-builder-pay.ts with tests

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
